# Line endings are pinned to LF for every text file in this project.
#
# Reason: the M2 review found scripts/m2-e2e.sh shipped with CRLF, and on Linux
# `bash -n` then failed with "syntax error near unexpected token `$'\r''".
# A shell script with CR line endings is broken on every non-Windows platform,
# and a Python shebang with a trailing CR fails with "bad interpreter".
#
# Normalising a file to LF changes nothing about its content; it only removes an
# accident of the editing environment. Set your editor to LF, or let Git do it:
#
#   git config core.autocrlf false        # repository-wide, for this checkout
#
# This file does NOT change any user's global Git configuration.
* text eol=lf

# Binary formats must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.key binary
*.pem binary
*.p12 binary

# Reports and font assets are binary; never normalize their bytes.
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Preserve historical receipts and paired report identities byte for byte.
verification/** -text
report/** -text

# Preserve original demonstration media bytes.
*.mp4 binary
*.MP4 binary
